{"question_id":"mnswhyj9","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift","year":2026,"subject":"physics","chapter":"wave-optics","chapterGroup":"optics","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>In Young's double slit experiment, the fringe width of the interference pattern produced on the screen is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.498ex\" height=\"2.186ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 3314 966\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1881,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. If the experiment is carried out in another medium having refractive index 1.2 , the fringe width will be <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.14ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.525ex\" height=\"0.084ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 25 2000 37\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.249ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 1436 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(603,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>1.2</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>2</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>2.4</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>2.88</p>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>In Young's Double Slit Experiment (YDSE), the fringe width ( <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ) is given by :</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.797ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.566ex\" height=\"2.798ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 3344.3 1236.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(850.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(1906.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(583,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D437\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D437\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(534,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><rect width=\"1197.7\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Where, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.319ex\" height=\"1.597ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 583 706\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is the wavelength of light used, D is the distance between the slits and the screen, and d is the distance between the two slits.</p>\n<p>When the experiment is moved from air/vacuum to a medium with a refractive index <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the speed of light decreases, which in turn decreases the wavelength. The new wavelength <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.947ex\" height=\"1.744ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -759 860.5 771\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(616,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.126ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.924ex\" height=\"3.128ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 3060.4 1382.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(616,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1138.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2194,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(227.1,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><rect width=\"626.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Since D and d are constant for the experimental setup, the new fringe width <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.038ex\" height=\"2.156ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -759 900.8 953\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(656.4,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> in the medium is :</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.126ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"27.688ex\" height=\"4.773ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1612.1 12237.9 2109.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\